# JOURNEY · the index: a player narrows the fishes to one species and sorts them by worth, from
# inside the table and from the command bar, and the table shows the command it is answering.
# The player buys Ann, a Koi, and Bea, a Merluza.

clear
include scenes/start-with-a-stake.play
include scenes/buy-a-fish.play Koi Ann
include scenes/buy-a-fish.play Merluza Bea
run /index
expect FishResource#index
expect Bea
expect Ann
key right
type f
type koi
expect /index species:koi
absent Merluza
expect Ann
snap the table narrows while the filter is typed
key enter
absent ENTER keep
expect C clear
type c
expect Bea
absent /index
key right
key right
type s
type s
expect Worth ▼
expect /index sort:-worth
snap the fishes by worth, the dearest first
key esc
absent FishResource#index
run /index species:koi sort:-worth
expect /index species:koi sort:-worth
expect Worth ▼
expect Ann
absent Merluza
snap the command bar asks the same question
key esc
